course: dictionary
lesson: 12039
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word circulation can mean the movement of blood around your body, the movement of air around a place, or things being passed from person to person. Context tells you which meaning to pick. Read the words around the word and ask: what is this sentence talking about?
explain: «Exercise is good for circulation.» Here circulation is about blood moving around your body, pumped by your heart. «The room needs better air circulation.» Here it is air moving around the room. The subject of the sentence tells you which meaning is right.
explain: «The new coins are now in circulation.» Here circulation means being used and passed from person to person. «The circulation of the newspaper went up this year» means how many copies were sold. Always check: does my meaning fit the sentence?
fact: Circulation means movement around a place, or around a body.
fact: Your heart pumps blood around your body; this is called blood circulation.
fact: «Good air circulation» means fresh air moves freely around a room.
fact: «In circulation» means being used or passed around, as with coins or money.
fact: The circulation of a newspaper or magazine is how many copies are sold.
exercise: «Cold fingers can mean poor circulation.» What does circulation mean here? | The movement of coins from person to person | *The movement of blood around your body | How many copies of a newspaper are sold
exercise: «The room needs better air circulation.» What does circulation mean here? | The movement of blood around the body | A large circle of friends | *The movement of air around a place | Money being passed round
exercise: «Old coins are no longer in circulation.» What does in circulation mean? | *Being used and passed around | Locked away in a museum | Made of pure gold | Lost at the bottom of the sea
test: Pick the meaning of circulation in «Exercise is good for circulation.» | Movement of air around a room | *Movement of blood around the body, pumped by the heart | People passing coins to each other
test: «The circulation of the magazine went up this month.» What does circulation mean here? | Coins being passed from hand to hand | *How many copies are sold | Air moving around a classroom | The movement of blood round the body
exam: «The old notes are out of circulation now.» What does out of circulation mean? | Air moving around the room | Being used and passed around | *No longer being used or passed around | Blood moving round the body
